cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Manifesto: protocols for digital existence — with a measured verifier-reported verification load"
abstract: >-
  An open ontology for digital entities (experience, responsibility,
  identity) that grew a measured research line. The earlier "reflexive
  verification bound" (a stability condition λ_G < (1−μ)λ_V with a phase
  transition at μ = 1) is RETIRED: its closed forms are refuted by scheduler
  counterexamples (papers/every-check-spawns-more, claim C6) and it is not a
  claim of this work. What is measured is ô, the verifier-reported offspring
  count per verification act, on a single LLM monologue corpus: ≈2–3 over
  sampled paths to depth 4 (finite-depth, not asymptotic) and ≈0.14 on
  termination controls; one claim compiled to a deterministic, budget-priced
  check has a terminal sub-act with zero emitted prose obligations, on a
  separate axis from ô (not "μ = 0"). Also: a settlement gate that catches
  generator hallucinations with priced receipts; an evidence pack; and the
  addressing-is-equality incident-and-repair note (a measured cost gap plus an
  executable soundness counterexample; equality by address holds only on an
  admitted profile, and the draft profile refuses the motivating case). Papers
  in papers/ carry claim ledgers with typed falsifiers and checkers that
  recount their figures from the repository. Nothing is deposited yet.
message: "If you use or evaluate this work, please cite it."
